      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nAcetaminophen 3,000 mg three times daily comes to 9,000 mg/day. The usual adult maximum is 4 g/day, and many institutions cap it at 3 g/day. A single 3,000 mg dose is also about three times the usual maximum of 1,000 mg. At 9 g/day, the risk of acute hepatotoxicity is serious, even with normal liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **1,000 mg PO three times daily** (3 g/day total)\n- **650 mg PO every 6 hours** (2.6 g/day)\n- **1,000 mg PO every 8 hours**, with a daily maximum of 3 g\n\nIf you do intend the 3,000 mg dose, tell me the clinical rationale and I'll review it with you. Otherwise, tell me which regimen you'd like and I'll enter it right away."
      }
