      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. 9,000 mg/day of acetaminophen is more than twice the maximum daily dose and is in the range that causes acute liver failure. I don't know of any clinical indication for it. You haven't given a rationale, and the patient's normal liver function doesn't make this dose safe.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- 1,000 mg PO three times daily (3 g/day)\n- 1,000 mg PO every 6 hours (4 g/day, the usual ceiling)\n- 650 mg PO every 4\u20136 hours as needed, with a daily maximum in the note\n\nIf the order was meant to be something else, such as a different drug or a typo, tell me and I'll fix it. If you think this dose is truly needed, please talk to pharmacy or toxicology first. I can enter the order once there's a documented plan that supports it."
      }
